**Version:** 2026.10.23. **Scope:** core CLI `update many --rollback` and exported `runUpdateMany`. **Severity:** high collaborative recovery risk. Live item evidence is removed; original events remain recoverable in append-only history. No permanent audit-log deletion is claimed.

Run this 17-line TypeScript reproduction in a fresh scratch npm package containing the pinned dependency, using `npx -y tsx repro.ts` with ESM enabled:

```ts
import { PmClient, runUpdateMany } from '@unbrained/pm-cli';
const c = new PmClient({ cwd: process.cwd(), author: 'codex-agent' });
await c.init(undefined, { defaults: true, agentGuidance: 'skip' });
const id = (await c.create({ type: 'Task', title: 'Original', priority: 2 })).item.id;
const g = { path: '.agents/pm', author: 'codex-agent' };
const batch = await runUpdateMany({ list: { ids: id },
  update: { priority: 0 } }, g);
const peer = new PmClient({ cwd: process.cwd(), author: 'peer-agent' });
await peer.comments(id, { add: 'New peer evidence after the batch' });
await peer.update(id, { title: 'Peer continued implementation', priority: 1 });
const before = await c.get(id, { full: true });
if (!batch.checkpoint) throw new Error('Missing checkpoint');
const rollback = await runUpdateMany({ list: {}, update: {},
  rollback: batch.checkpoint.id }, g);
const after = await c.get(id, { full: true });
console.log(before.item.title, before.item.comments, rollback);
console.log(after.item.title, after.item.priority, after.item.comments);
```

**Observed:** after rollback the title is `Original`, priority is 2 and comments are empty. Rollback returns effect/exit 0 with no warnings. Its changed_fields includes comments/title even though the original batch changed only priority. A separate two-item CLI reproduction agrees: priority-only apply → peer comment → peer title update → actual rollback removes the later title/comment. `--dry-run --rollback` is refused, so there is no successful rollback preview to warn about these losses.

The per-item failure control additionally showed that the checkpoint includes an item whose forward update failed. Rollback restores that item too and removes its subsequent comment, despite the batch never having changed that row successfully.

**Expected:** undo only the successful batch effects. Preserve unrelated later fields and annotations; use an inverse patch guarded by the batch's postimage/fingerprint. When a changed field itself has drifted, return a conflict with an explicit resolution path. If whole-item restoration is intentional, require explicit acknowledgement and expose the affected later edits before overwriting them. Failed rows should not be restored as if their forward mutation succeeded.

**Measured cost:** actual CLI rollback receipt **964 bytes / 241 tokens**, 30.538 seconds, followed by a **1,260-byte / 315-token** projected state read, 24.348 seconds: **two calls / 556 tokens** to execute and discover the unrelated losses. The response reports restored rows and empty warnings, not the post-checkpoint edits it discards. The independent SDK control observes the same state change. These timings are host observations, not intrinsic operation latency.

**Duplicate searches:** each used `gh issue list -R unbraind/pm-cli --state all --search '<query>' --limit 20`:

- `"rollback" "comment"`
- `"update-many" "rollback"`
- `"rollback" "drift"`
- `"rollback" "concurrent"`
- `"bulk" "rollback" "drift"`
- `"close-many" "rollback"`
- `"rollback" "overwrite"`

No matching per-item bulk rollback report found. **#812** was read: it concerns whole-workspace snapshot restore truncating histories and removing items; this reproduction never invokes workspace restore and retains history. **#613** is the general atomic item-mutation helper, **#1370/#256** concern preview semantic validation, and **#1545** concerns failed package replacement. None describes this rollback overwriting unrelated later item edits. Searches of probes 5/6 and the named excluded issues found no overlapping draft.



Re-verified independently by the orchestrator on 2026.10.23 with the TypeScript reproduction above: after rollback the item reads `Original 2 []` (peer title, priority and comment lost).
